Issue Bodies:
We should be able to see/reach relevant logs from the metrics app.Design Doc: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vFqk-Cs_zw5vR-TkuhLI85Fa0709YV07tc3hzIGZtlA/editPhase 1: PoC to show logs only for Loki recording rules https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/94656Tasks to ship PoC:- [x] Basic functionality  - [x] Add a Related Logs tab  - [x] Fetch Loki Recording Rules associated with selected metric  - [x] Add selector for data sources with Recording Rules for the selected metric  - [x] Display logs associated with Recording Rules for the active Loki data source- [x] [Bug] When we switch to logs tab, we send two loki queries. It must be one. Bug found in [commit](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/94656/commits/2ff65305e2b751474c18ebf0f0bb2931442d3a38). Bug fixed in https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/94656/commits/44e868d49fc07f5408e5c4c5432f0e8ab9b58d01.- [x] Show a help message when there are no logs for the selected metric- [x] Add a button to open logs view in explore-logs and connect the button with extension link- [x] Put logs integration behind a feature flag and enable it for internal users- [ ] Instrument the feature (`'metric_action_view_changed': 'related-logs'`, `'related_logs_action_clicked': 'open_explore_logs'`)- [ ] Create an [extension point](https://grafana.com/developers/plugin-tools/key-concepts/ui-extensions) to go [Explore Logs](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/latest/explore/simplified-exploration/logs)- [x] Write unit tests- [ ] Write e2e tests (do we even have e2e tests for explore apps?)- [x] ~~A rule might be defined under two different rule groups. Find a way to handle this situation.~~ We'll handle this in a better way in Phase 2  - [x] Display only the logs of the first rule. - [ ] Enable fullstory integration (if it is not yet enabled) for the feature | ### What happened?When during dashbaord variable value lookup (label_values function call) Grafana sends requests to Prometheus datasource  `x-datasource-uid`  header isn't attached to http request sent to Prometheus### What did you expect to happen?Assumptions was that Grafana will always send `x-datasource-uid` and `x-grafana-org-id` headers to prometheus for all api calls.### Did this work before?No idea ### How do we reproduce it?1. Spin up new Grafana v11.2.0 instance1. Configure Grafana to use OKTA 1. Log in into Grafana UI1. Crete new Prometheus datasoruce point it to `http://127.0.0.1:7500` 1. Create new Dashbaord 1. Create dummy pannel with prometheus query `up`1. Start dummy http server `nc -l 7500`- just to capture raw http request 1. Refresh dummy pannel  - `x-datasource-uid` and `x-grafana-org-id` are present in NC output1. Add dashboard variable based on dummy datasource1.1. Type - classic query1.2. query  - `label_valies(up,instance)`1. Run variable query1. Chek NC ouptu - observe missing `x-datasource-uid` header### Is the bug inside a dashboard panel?no### Environment (with versions)?Grafana: v11.2.0OS: Amazon Linux 2023Browser: Windows 11 Vivaldi | 6.9.3447.48### Grafana platform?A downloaded binary### Datasource(s)?_No response_ | Sometimes, the graph on a metric select page does not seem to match the graph when you click into the metric.See video: https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3cf25aba-75f4-4725-82e8-30d053a20cf9I've only noticed this on the mythical-app data source, but not any other ones | **What is this feature?**Fix so incremental querying behaves the same as normal querying.**Why do we need this feature?**Prevents unexpected "gap" in panels between the y-axis and the first datapoint.**Who is this feature for?**Users of prometheus incremental querying**Which issue(s) does this PR fix?**:Fixes https://github.com/grafana/support-escalations/issues/12304**Special notes for your reviewer:**Please check that:- [ ] It works as expected from a user's perspective.- [ ] If this is a pre-GA feature, it is behind a feature toggle.- [ ] The docs are updated, and if this is a [notable improvement](https://grafana.com/docs/writers-toolkit/contribute/release-notes/#how-to-determine-if-content-belongs-in-whats-new), it's added to our [What's New](https://grafana.com/docs/writers-toolkit/contribute/release-notes/) doc. | We went through a Bug Bash and will prioritize these items for the Explore Metrics GA (September Patching cut-off: Sept. 20)[Bug bash doc](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ABXhrwDAXj_z-X9PQsEZ_uBKceOhY2zzCw0fZbQw_zU/edit#heading=h.bi9y12rx0lgs )```[tasklist]### Tasks in prioritized order- [ ] https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/92411- [ ] https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/92413- [ ] https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/93073- [ ] https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/92414- [ ] https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/92415- [ ] https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/91510- [ ] https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/92416- [ ] https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/92417``` | Sometimes we get errors that are not json and `jsoniter` breaks like this```ReadObject: expect { or , or } or n, but found u, error found in #1 byte of ...|unexpected |..., bigger context ...|unexpected error |...(Trace ID: 0000e63fb664a14cd0fdcc070c6d9b78) ```We can check that the response is json before running `jsoniter` and parse the error as what it is. | ### What happened?We have many metrics with empty graphs in the Explore Metrics section.For some metrics the panel works just fine, but for others it is empty.Tried to debug. Opened the query in explore and I found it is using` $__rate_interval`. In may case it was:`sum(rate(jvm_cpu_time_seconds_total{}[$__rate_interval]))`The issue is that we are scrapping every 30 seconds. That query just does not work. It starts working though if I open the time windows to 24h or similar. There I get what I was looking for.In the regular explore I can modify the query or change the step interval, etc, but when it comes to the Explore Metrics section I cannot do any of that, leaving lots of metrics unusable for periods shorter that 24h or so.### What did you expect to happen?I expect to get the values plotted in the graphics.### Did this work before?Never was working.### How do we reproduce it?In my case some JVM metrics are not coming up. See picture.![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cf79a1b6-42fa-43e7-a025-35608f17d1af)Opening the windows to 24h works fine![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/47dbf4eb-138e-4a50-b0f6-c8e1498be9c5)### Is the bug inside a dashboard panel?_No response_### Environment (with versions)?Grafana: 11.2.0Under docker 23.0.5, on Debian 11### Grafana platform?Docker### Datasource(s)?_No response_ | - When seeing all labels, after selecting “rows” view the url reflects that and we switched to the rows view. After that if we select a label it switches to the three option view (single, grid, rows), but in the group “grid” is selected where “rows” should be selected. Also URL is still showing as ”rows”. - When seeing one label and selecting “rows” and going back the the all labels is switching view as “grid”. | See:https://raintank-corp.slack.com/archives/C0630AYC4SY/p1708936490386859?thread_ts=1708729435.077859&cid=C0630AYC4SYThere is a bug where some job and namespace values are showing under the route label![Image](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/5264102/d1e58703-bf1c-423a-b186-64a0b581340a)To replicate:Data source: dev-cortexMetric: job_route_cluster:pyroscope_request_duration_seconds_bucket:sum_rateIf you go under breakdown --> look at the aggregated route graph you can see job values like dev-us-east-0 or namespace values. However they do not show when you select the route label, and view each value.- Different aggregations (irate, increase) - I believe there's another issue for this | `lezer-promql` support UTF-8 labels. See: https://github.com/prometheus/prometheus/pull/13590`parsing.ts` and `situation.ts` should also support new changes. In this PR (https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/91252) we only made the changes for backward compatibility.  | Changepoint detection was implemented in Logs App https://github.com/grafana/explore-logs/pull/512More context: https://raintank-corp.slack.com/archives/C0630AYC4SY/p1721317541867459 | This can just be an icon similar to the rest of the other action buttons in explore metrics. Let's have it after the Explore button, and before the Share button.![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4c1229fd-8d25-4110-8b8c-28586be2a2a5)We will need to make sure there is tracking on this button click | Around 24% of explore metric users interact with the trail history, however there is limited information in the tooltip to help users navigate through the dots.This aims to provide more information for users to effectively use the trail breadcrumbs![Image](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/5264102/fe6ce140-42ee-4d1c-ad22-ba07a2e9a61e)Figma file: https://www.figma.com/design/eL7u2QrvLykWRLeUELiNNy/%5BGA%5D-Explore-Metrics---Master-File?node-id=718-44076&t=SvV55zI1cpKhJvA9-1(UX ticket: https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/89506)  | After selecting a metric, in the overview tab, if the metric has a lot of labels, while scrolling down the labels are being visible behind the panel. ![Image](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/820946/842e140b-9f09-4fed-9a44-bcbb7701108d) | ### What happened?I went to explore, added a query in prometheus datasource, used "both" type of query (range and instant), switched to mixed datasource, hid the query, but the instant results didn't disappear.![image](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/1511481/d0aef7a8-f86e-4080-8cc8-b2b6a408c398)### What did you expect to happen?I expected hidden queries to be hidden.### Did this work before?No idea.### How do we reproduce it?1. Go to explore by pressing `g` `e`. ![image](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/1511481/908c1f26-2e0a-4574-aaee-9c4bae45279a)2. Make sure a Prometheus datasource is selected and query type is "both".3. Write a query and observe both range and instant results. ![image](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/1511481/26bb6da6-0f0b-4f32-83e8-cd1c531ae31a)4. Switch to mixed datasource. ![image](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/1511481/586171bd-5a00-426a-9ac7-b2bc87f085f4)5. Hide the query, observe that range query results hide, but not the instant ones. ![image](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/1511481/9974459d-e200-4506-b42e-324361398dd8)### Is the bug inside a dashboard panel?No.### Environment (with versions)?Our internal ops.grafana-ops.netGrafana: Grafana v11.2.0-72495 (b1ce7e8a83)OS: MacBrowser: Arc 1.49### Grafana platform?I use Grafana Cloud### Datasource(s)?Prometheus | Examples:![Image](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/5264102/ed75bb46-aeca-4d81-9915-981dde500671)![Image](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/5264102/bd7bfaf6-8b6f-44e7-a3ed-f10ff7b3e0c0)![Image](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/5264102/ce672325-eff4-486b-8e72-9b39a83a303e)Here is a document that discusses many of our problems with units.https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lk7SKP9zHJnj2mjvLwHF5ZL6P4HTkCM7f8FxGQh7slk/edit | There are a couple of approaches we could try to display metrics. Currently, we display all of the metrics in alphabetical order. We can use name grouping![Image](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/820946/43f7cd3c-f6a4-428a-b714-84562ca0224b)We can use tab grouping ![Image](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/820946/ffcee412-23f2-4dff-9365-f6add4acb071)We can use dropdown filtering ![Image](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/820946/11f2bc18-06ea-4432-875f-3cde299f9214)The goal is to implement all three (maybe more in the future) in a PoC and let stakeholders explore. | ### What happened?Query parse error when using ad hoc filters and native histograms```bad_data: invalid parameter "query": 2:2: parse error: unexpected right parenthesis ')'```<img width="950" alt="image" src="https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/1