ame query I use to retrieve the variable values _does_ work in the data explorer, so it's specific to flux query variables.Others also have this issue, see my [Grafana Community Forum post](https://community.grafana.com/t/time-range-values-not-passed-to-variable-queries/123269)It may be related to https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/88642### What did you expect to happen?Load the unique tag values from the provided tag in the provided time range.### Did this work before?Yes, it fails since June 4 or 5. It worked fine before on this same dashboard. Nothing changed in the datasource or dashboard.### How do we reproduce it?1. Create an InfluxDB datasource with some measurements with a tag with varying values2. Create a dashboard variable with my above query (alter the bucket and tag names)3. Try to use variable in a dashboard visualization.4. Check the HTTP requests sent in your browser tools### Is the bug inside a dashboard panel?_No response_### Environment (with versions)?Grafana: Grafana v11.1.0-71516 (0ba54152dc)OS: MacOS Sonoma 14.5 (23F79)Browser: Safari (bug is not browser-specific)### Grafana platform?I use Grafana Cloud### Datasource(s)?InfluxDB v2.7.4 | <!-- Please only use this template for submitting feature requests -->**Why is this needed**:When Explore-ing a Prometheus datasource, it fetches all rules via the /api/v1/rules API, to be able to expand recording rules. It is possible the datasource has a huge number of alerts in addition to recording rules, making this API call very slow and return a lot of data.**What would you like to be added**:Prometheus and derivatives (e.g. Mimir) have an option on this API to only fetch recording rules, this would make the API call faster and potentially return substantially less data.The API call should be: `/api/v1/rules?type=record`**Who is this feature for?**Users of Explore with Prometheus data sources. | ### What happened?![Grafana Auto Step Bug](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/3635576/bd856eff-8bac-4c7a-ac80-7dbe42c05be0)Using explore mode, if you pick a short time window for your query, such as 15m, and use a -- Mixed -- datasource with a Prometheus datasource for your actual expression, it will pick a very short step value which is different to the default prometheus step value. In the example in the screenshot above, the left hand panel is a "regular" prometheus datasource which defaults to a 30s step. On the righthand side, all I've done is changed the datasource to -- Mixed -- and it has picked a 1s step instead.### What did you expect to happen?I expected that the same step would be picked whether the datasource is -- Mixed -- or not.### Did this work before?Unknown### How do we reproduce it?1. In the Explore page, pick a Prometheus datasource, and a 15m time window.2. Ensure that the Step field is blank so that an automatic value is picked3. You are likely to see a datapoint at every 30s interval4. Click on the Query inspector and pick the JSON tab.5. Search for the Step value and it will likely be 30s.6. Now change the datasource type to -- Mixed -- and ensure that the correct datasource is selected for the actual expression7. Now look again at the data and you'll see more regular datapoints8. If you search the json data again for the step it will not be 30s, and may be as small as 500ms (as appeared during one of my tests) or 1s.### Is the bug inside a dashboard panel?no### Environment (with versions)?Grafana: 11.0.0OS: macOS 14.5Browser: Microsoft Edge 125### Grafana platform?Kubernetes### Datasource(s)?Prometheus v2.46.0 | **What is this feature?** Upgrande promethues/prometheus dependency to v0.52.0**Why do we need this feature?**Support new native histogram function in the parser, which is hit when promQLScope feature flag is enabled.**Special notes for your reviewer:** - Need alerting to verify that the changes in sender.go for service discovery are right, as I'm just copying what I see elsewhere and don't have the context.Please check that:- [ ] It works as expected from a user's perspective.- [ ] If this is a pre-GA feature, it is behind a feature toggle.- [ ] The docs are updated, and if this is a [notable improvement](https://grafana.com/docs/writers-toolkit/writing-guide/contribute-release-notes/#how-to-determine-if-content-belongs-in-a-whats-new-document), it's added to our [What's New](https://grafana.com/docs/writers-toolkit/writing-guide/contribute-release-notes/) doc. | The global variable check was introduced here https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/60461So when we are writing promql if we use `$__rate_interval` or `$__interval` the query will stay valid. But the way we provide this check is not performant. It iterates twice. We should be able to detect this in one go. Since the [lezer package was upgraded](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/85942) to the latest version we are able to implement a better solution.  | ### What happened?FWIW - I'm writing this up after discussing a customer's experience with @itsmylifeI was looking at an Mimir alert rule definition, and chose to "Explore" the query. The Explore GUI detected that the query was referring to a recorded series and suggested I could "expand rules", which I did. The results weren't what I expected because I have more than one recording rule that writes into the metric name, each made unique by additional prometheus labels on the recorded series.### What did you expect to happen?I expected the "expand rules" function to find the rule that populated the series I was querying or to give me some kind of warning / error that it found multiple matches and might not work for me query.I also expected the result of the "expand rules" action to be a promql query that no longer contained the `uuid=...` label matcher, because that label was added as the result of the recording rule and didn't exist in the raw metrics (i.e. I can't run the expression from the rule AND include the "uuid" label matcher, that uuid label won't exist on the raw metrics, only the recorded series)https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/5599664/90acfd75-0081-4d52-b6f7-d41d8b876773### Did this work before?No, I don't think this worked before. I chose to write it up as a bug rather than a feature request, because I thought it would be easier to understand the issue this way.### How do we reproduce it?1. Produce multiple recording rules that write to the same metric name (ex: `recorded_series`) , where each adds labels to the rule object (ex: `uuid=<unique value per rule>`)2. Explore a promql query like `recorded_series{uuid="foo"}` and click "expand rules" 3. Confirm that the expanded query comes from the first recording rule that matches metric name `recorded_series` rather than from the one that had `rule.Labels[uuid] = "foo"`### Is the bug inside a dashboard panel?no. It's in the Explore GUI### Environment (with versions)?Grafana: 11.1.0OS: CloudBrowser: chrome### Grafana platform?I use Grafana Cloud### Datasource(s)?prometheus | Here is a sample dashboard json from play.grafana.org.[Grafana Play Home-1713286423719.json](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/files/15000154/Grafana.Play.Home-1713286423719.json)![image](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/820946/7ae00ce7-f790-404b-b52a-14bae2380621)`Resolution => 1.0` | ### What happened?When using a repeated panel there's no data returned if using Editor Mode with the $Variable in the SELECT query. However it works in Raw Query Mode. ### What did you expect to happen?There should be data returned for either Raw Query Mode or Editor Mode.### Did this work before?Worked in 10.2.2### How do we reproduce it?1.  Create a dashboard with a variable to InfluxDB data. For example create a variables `Sensors` which returns all fields in a measurement (`SHOW FIELD KEYS FROM x` where x is the measurement)2. Create a panel querying Influx data with `Repeat by variable` on `Sensors`3. In the Panel SELECT field use `$Sensors`4. No data will be returned5. Switch to Raw Query Mode, data is returned.### Is the bug inside a dashboard panel?_No response_### Environment (with versions)?Grafana Cloud: 11.1.0Grafana OpenSource: 10.4.2, 10.4.1 (docker image grafana/grafana)Browser: Chrome### Grafana platform?I use Grafana Cloud### Datasource(s)?InfluxDB | Use lezer-promql-tree-viz -> https://github.com/grafana/lezer-promql-tree-vizUpdate lezer packages ```"@lezer/common": "1.2.1","@lezer/highlight": "1.2.0","@lezer/lr": "1.4.0",```Update `@prometheus-io/lezer-promql` package https://www.npmjs.com/package/@prometheus-io/lezer-promql | ### What happened?Hello,I am using Grafana 10 and influxdb v2.7.4.I am using below flux code to create grafana variable for my dashboard.When i test this on influxdb script editor, i can get 3500 Client_Name variable values.But when i apply this as a variable and open the variable filter on dashboard the values are truncated. In alphabetic order i can only get until variable names starting with f… Nearly %70 of the variable value Client Names are missing in the filter. If i open variable configuring page. If i create variable from influx v2.7.4, i can only see 1000 client names at variable creation page by preview of values section at bottom of page.I also have same data on influxdb 1.8 version. If i create variable from influx 1.8 with influxql, i can see 3500 client names at variable creation page by preview of values section at bottom of page.Below shows that 3500 clients are coming in the filter with variable from influxdb 1.8 version with influxql.![image](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/52052330/15c89b33-64f9-40ea-9ab2-13b547723cfb)But if i create variable from v2.7.4 influxdb with flux only 1000 clients are shown or searched.Below shows v2.7.4 same data.![image](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/52052330/c412c8bd-4273-4777-b7d3-95d51a92f8f0)Note : Tests are done with same 3500 Client_Name data in influxdb 1.8 and influxdb 2.7.4.1) If i create variable from influx 2.7.4 with flux with below query only 1000 client names are shown at preview area at variable creation page (Also in dashboard filter):import "influxdata/influxdb/schema"schema.tagValues(    bucket: "VFBckStrg",    tag: "Client_Name")2) If i create variable from influx 1.8 with influxql with below query all 3500 client names are shown at preview area at variable creation page (Also in dashboard filter):SHOW TAG VALUES FROM “SELECTBOX_VALUES” WITH KEY = “Client_Name”### What did you expect to happen?When I create a Grafana variable with influxql in InfluxDB version 1.8, I can search and find all 3500 clients in the dashboard filter using this variable. However, in InfluxDB version 2.7.4, when I create a variable with flux, I can only list and search for the first 1000 clients in the filter. If I can find each of the 3500 clients in the dashboard filter with InfluxDB 1.8, I want to be able to find each of the 3500 clients in the Grafana variable filter created with the newer version, InfluxDB v2.7.4, using the flux language. I suspect there is an issue with variable integration in Grafana using InfluxDB v2.7 and the flux language.### Did this work before?When I create a Grafana 10 variable with influxql in InfluxDB version 1.8, I can search and find all 3500 clients in the dashboard filter using this variable. However, in InfluxDB version 2.7.4, when I create a variable with flux, I can only list and search for the first 1000 clients in the filter.### How do we reproduce it?1. Create data with **Client_Name** tag with **3500 sample tag values** on **influxdb 1.8** version.2. Create data with **Client_Name** tag with **3500 sample tag values** on **influxdb 2.7.4** version.3. Create grafana variable named XVAR with influxdb 1.8 with Client_Name tag with below influxql query :     SHOW TAG VALUES FROM “SELECTBOX_VALUES” WITH KEY = “Client_Name”    Preview values on variable page and see 3500 values are shown.4. Create grafana variable named ZVAR with influxdb 2.7.4 with Client_Name tag with below FLUX query :import "influxdata/influxdb/schema"schema.tagValues(    bucket: "VFBckStrg",    tag: "Client_Name")Preview values on variable page and see only 1000 values are shown.5. Open dashboard and check XVAR filter. You will be able to search and get all 3500 tag values in the fil
